AArch64 GussetParkWakeDekkerDisproofNoFence
"Disproof companion (`Sometimes`) to `park_wake_dekker.litmus`:
 omits the worker's `DMB ISH` (`fence(Ordering::SeqCst)`) between publishing
 `STLR X0, [seq]` and reading `LDR W2, [waiting]`.

 Without `DMB ISH`, `[Exp & W & L]; po; [Exp & R]` has no `bob` edge in
 `aarch64hwreqs.cat`, permitting StoreLoad reordering and lost wake (`0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0`).

 Expected `herd7` verdict under `aarch64.cat`: `Sometimes`."
{
  uint64_t seq = 0;
  uint32_t waiting = 0;
  0:X0=1; 0:X1=seq; 0:X3=waiting;
  1:X0=1; 1:X1=waiting; 1:X3=seq;
}
 P0                       | P1                       ;
 STLR X0, [X1]            | SWPAL W0, W2, [X1]       ;
 LDR W2, [X3]             | LDAR X4, [X3]            ;
exists (0:X2=0 /\ 1:X4=0)
